description:
Write a class `Finally` that takes any function in its constructor and runs it in its destructor. It turns "remember to do X on the way out" into something the compiler remembers for you.

- `explicit Finally(std::function<void()> action)`
- `void dismiss()`: cancels the action, so the destructor does nothing.
- Not copyable.

```cpp
{
    Finally cleanup{ [&] { log += "bye"; } };
    // ... anything, including early returns ...
}   // "bye" is appended here
```

